label: Soil Polygon WKT
description: >-
  One soil map-unit polygon, already clipped to the parcel BY THE SERVER, as
  SDA returns it: a mukey and a WKT string.

  Worth pinning down, because modelling it made it obvious and it was not
  obvious before: the CLIP happens at USDA
  (`mupolygongeo.STIntersection(...)`, ssurgo.ts:44), not locally. See
  measureSoilPolygon.node for why that matters.
index: polygonId
fields:
  polygonId:
    type: utf8
    label: Polygon ID
    description: >-
      Stable key for this clipped segment. SDA returns one row per
      mukey/segment and a single mukey can produce several disjoint segments
      within one parcel, so mukey alone is NOT a key -- blue-ribbon discovers
      this implicitly by summing per mukey afterwards.
    nullable: false
    validations:
      minLength: 1
      maxLength: 100
  mukey:
    type: utf8
    label: Map Unit Key
    description: SSURGO map unit this segment belongs to
    nullable: false
    validations:
      minLength: 1
      maxLength: 30
  wkt:
    type: utf8
    label: WKT
    description: The clipped polygon geometry, as SDA returned it
    nullable: false
    validations:
      minLength: 10
      maxLength: 1000000
